# ML Module Details — VoiceUp Decision Support

## Overview

This document provides the detailed internal explanation of the `sarma_ml` module used in the VoiceUp project.

The purpose of this module is to support the larger VoiceUp Decision Support System by providing a machine learning pipeline for complaint text understanding, classification, text severity scoring, evaluation, and research graph generation.

This ML module focuses specifically on the **text-analysis part** of the project.

It is responsible for:

- generating a realistic complaint dataset
- creating text variations for better robustness
- splitting the dataset into train / validation / test sets
- training TF-IDF based classification models
- training an ML-based text severity scoring model
- validating model performance
- generating research graphs for the research paper
- saving trained artifacts for backend integration

The final system is **not fully automated**.  
The ML output is only one part of the full hybrid pipeline.  
The backend combines:

- ML-based text severity
- GIS context scoring
- recurring complaint analysis

to generate a final hybrid priority score.  
The final decision is still made by the responsible officer.

---

## Project Role of This Module

In the full VoiceUp architecture, this folder provides the **ML text intelligence layer**.

### The ML module supports:
- complaint understanding from text
- category prediction
- sub-category prediction
- priority support prediction
- text severity prediction

### The backend then combines ML output with:
- GIS-based spatial evidence
- recurrence evidence
- rule-based and structured decision support logic

So this module is part of a **Decision Support System**, not an autonomous decision engine.

---

## Main Purpose of Each File

### `dataset_templated_sa.py`
This file contains the structured complaint templates used to generate the training dataset.

Each template defines:
- main category
- sub-category
- priority level
- severity score
- base complaint sentences

This file acts as the base supervision source for synthetic dataset generation.

---

### `text_variation_utils_sa.py`
This file creates realistic text variations from template complaints.

It applies:
- synonyms
- filler phrases
- prefixes and suffixes
- typo injection
- ambiguity injection
- optional keyword removal
- expanded text generation

This helps create more realistic complaint text samples instead of only using rigid template sentences.

---

### `generate_training_dataset_sa.py`
This script generates the full labeled complaint dataset.

It:
- reads template definitions
- creates multiple complaint text variations
- creates expanded complaint text
- assigns labels
- assigns text severity score
- writes the final dataset into CSV format

Output:
- `complaints_training_sa.csv`

---

### `split_dataset_sa.py`
This script splits the generated dataset into:
- training set
- validation set
- test set

It uses stratified splitting to preserve label balance as much as possible.

Output:
- `complaints_train_sa.csv`
- `complaints_val_sa.csv`
- `complaints_test_sa.csv`

---

### `train_models_sa.py`
This script trains the TF-IDF based classification models.

These models predict:
- `main_category`
- `sub_category`
- `priority_level`

Algorithm used:
- TF-IDF vectorizer
- Logistic Regression

Output artifacts:
- `tfidf_vectorizer.joblib`
- classification models
- label encoders

---

### `validate_models_sa.py`
This script evaluates the complaint classification models on the validation set.

It reports:
- classification accuracy
- classification report
- label-wise evaluation

This is used to measure the quality of the classification pipeline.

---

### `train_text_severity_model_sa.py`
This script trains a separate ML model to predict **numeric text severity score**.

This model is used for:
- text-based severity estimation
- hybrid priority scoring input

Algorithm used:
- TF-IDF vectorizer
- Ridge Regression

Output artifacts:
- `tfidf_vectorizer_severity.joblib`
- `text_severity_model.joblib`

---

### `validate_text_severity_model_sa.py`
This script validates the text severity prediction model.

It reports:
- MAE
- RMSE
- R²
- bucket accuracy (Low / Medium / High)

This script is important for the research evaluation section.

---

### `generate_research_graphs_sa.py`
This script creates visual graphs from the text severity validation results.

It generates:
- validation performance bar chart
- actual vs predicted scatter plot
- bucket confusion matrix

These graphs are useful in the **Results / Evaluation** section of the research paper.

---

## What the ML Module Predicts

This module performs two types of ML tasks.

### 1. Complaint Classification
Using complaint text, the model predicts:

- `main_category`  
  Example: road / garbage

- `sub_category`  
  Example: access_mobility, health_risk, infrastructure_gap, etc.

- `priority_level`  
  Example: Level 1 / Level 2 / Level 3

These outputs are used as **supporting predictions**.

---

### 2. Text Severity Prediction
A separate model predicts:

- `severity_score`

This is a numeric value representing the seriousness of the complaint text itself.

This score is used as the **text component** inside the hybrid priority scoring pipeline.

---

## Data Flow of the ML Module

### Complaint text processing flow

```text
Complaint Text
    ↓
Preprocessing / Text Variation
    ↓
TF-IDF Vectorization
    ↓
ML Model
    ↓
Prediction

